### Query the list of user groups under a hierarchical administrator

> You can only query the list of user groups under a hierarchical administrator


#### Parameters

| Field | Type | Required | Location | Description |
| --------|--------|--------|--------|--------|
| id | int | yes | path | Grade manager ID |
| page_size | int | Yes | query | One of the paging query parameters, page_size indicates the number of queries, `maximum is 100` |
| page | int | Yes | query | One of the paging query parameters, page means the number of pages to be queried, page starts from 0 |

#### Response

| Field | Type | Description |
| -----------|-----------|-----------|
| count | int | Total number |
| results | array[object] | Paginated query results |

**results**
| Field | Type | Description |
| -----------|-----------|-----------|
| id | int | User group ID |
| name | string | User group name |
| description | string | User group description |
| apply_disable | bool | User group application disabled |
| attributes | array[object] | User group attributes |

**attributes**
| Field | Type | Description |
| -----------|-----------|-----------|
| readonly | bool | The user group is read-only. If true, the user group cannot be deleted on the IAM (Identity and Access Management) product |

```json
{
 "code": 0,
 "message": "ok",
 "data": {
   "count": 3,
   "results": [
